                  <provenance type="#b"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church.
                        </orgName><p>(fol. 423v) 'Byblia quondam in custodia magistri Iohannis
                        Langdon . . . In custodia W. Bonyngton anno domini 1483 et R
                        primo'.</p><p>John Langdon was a Canterbury monk professed in 1465, who died
                        in 1496 having been twice the warden of Canterbury College (1478--82,
                        1486--95) (see Greatrex 217--18), William Bonyngton professed at Christ
                        Church in 1469 and died 1485 (Greatrex 95).</p></provenance>
